/**
 * Paintable St. Francis Xavier, built from the supplied line art
 * (1024 x 1536, traced with potrace).
 *
 * Expected parent SVG viewBox: 0 0 640 760
 *
 * Every region below is snapped to the compartments of the line art itself —
 * each compartment takes the region covering most of it — so every boundary
 * lands exactly on a line the artist drew, and nothing bleeds past an outline.
 *
 * Two things are deliberate. The clouds share the background region: they are
 * drawn as open scallop chains rather than closed shapes, so there is no
 * outline to fill them against and they read as line work over the sky. And
 * the horizon, the shoreline and the island's silhouette are cut along curves
 * read off the drawing, because the sky, the sea and the open ground are one
 * unbroken compartment in the art.
 *
 * None of these paths may carry stroke="none". SaintArt gives each paint region
 * a stroke in its own colour precisely to close the hairline gaps that traced
 * masks leave along an outline; suppressing it leaves a thread of background
 * between every fill and its line, and those threads read as the background
 * region, so tapping one repaints the whole sky.
 *
 * The ink is drawn last with pointerEvents disabled.
 */

const ART_TRANSFORM =
  'matrix(0.4557291667 0 0 0.4557291667 86.6666666667 0)';

